# Unity C#

- Follow patterns already in the domain folders under `Assets/` rather than introducing a new architecture.
- Use Unity 6 / standard `MonoBehaviour` style unless the user asks for something else.
- Keep scripts small and named for what they do. Do not rename files just to match a style guide.
- No paid-power, cheat, or debug-win shortcuts in shipping gameplay code.
- Prefer data on ScriptableObjects or similar assets once a roster exists; do not hardcode a fake unit list.
